---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About this publication and the person behind it.">
  <article class="about-page">
    <header>
      <p class="index-label">About · Index 02</p>
      <h1>A place for<br /><em>unfinished ideas.</em></h1>
    </header>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p class="lead">Hello, I’m {site.author}. I use this space to think slowly about fast-moving things.</p>
      <p>I’m interested in the point where technology becomes understandable—where a complicated system can be explained clearly, where an interface becomes quiet enough to support thought, and where fewer moving parts create more room for meaningful work.</p>

      <h2>Why this place exists</h2>
      <p>The internet makes publishing effortless, but thoughtful writing still asks for time and attention. MiniBlog is where I keep that attention: a public notebook for ideas that are still forming, experiments that taught me something, and questions worth returning to.</p>
      <p>It is not a portfolio of finished answers. It is a record of learning in motion. Writing here helps me turn vague impressions into clearer ideas—and leaves a trail that someone else might find useful.</p>

      <h2>What I care about</h2>
      <p>I write about technology, engineering, design, AI, and the craft of building small systems. Across those subjects, I keep returning to the same concerns: clarity over cleverness, quality without excess, and tools that help people understand rather than merely impress them.</p>

      <h2>How it is built</h2>
      <p>This site follows the same principles it writes about. It aims for a mature reading experience without hiding behind unnecessary technical complexity. Every decision sits between a complexity budget and a quality floor: simple enough to understand, complete enough to feel intentional.</p>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>You can follow the source, experiments, and future iterations on <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a>. If an idea here gives you a useful question, the site has done its job.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
